/**
 * Era VI — The Galaxies (13.8 → 100 billion years).
 *
 * The home galaxy's group, seen from far above. Fling galaxies: close passes raise tidal tails and
 * starbursts; slow meetings end in mergers, which turn spirals into ellipticals, sink their black
 * holes together and light quasars. Dark energy carries everything outside the group's bound region
 * away; fling it back in or lose it beyond the horizon. The era ends with one giant galaxy, alone.
 */
